CaloriQ - Steps To Run Locally

1) Prerequisites
- Python 3.11+ installed
- Flutter SDK installed and on PATH
- Android Studio SDK / platform tools installed (adb)
- Ollama installed
- Git (optional)

2) Start Ollama and pull Qwen model (one-time)
- ollama pull qwen2.5:4b
- Optional test:
  ollama run qwen2.5:4b "Reply with exactly: QWEN_OK"

3) Backend setup
- Open terminal in project root
- cd backend
- Create venv if needed:
  python -m venv .venv
- Activate venv (PowerShell):
  .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
- Install dependencies:
  pip install -r requirements.txt

4) Backend environment
Create backend/.env with:
- ENABLE_QWEN=true
- QWEN_STRICT=true
- QWEN_TIMEOUT_SEC=15
- OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
- QWEN_MODEL=qwen2.5:4b
- OCR_PRIMARY_ENGINE=easyocr

Optional PaddleOCR setup:
- pip install paddleocr paddlepaddle
- To make PaddleOCR primary, set:
  OCR_PRIMARY_ENGINE=paddleocr
- Supported values:
  easyocr | pytesseract | paddleocr | auto

5) Run backend
- In backend folder with venv active:
  python app.py
- Backend should be available at:
  http://127.0.0.1:5000
- Health check:
  http://127.0.0.1:5000/health

6) Run Flutter app with USB (recommended for development)
- Open new terminal
- cd flutter_app
- flutter pub get
- Connect phone via USB
- adb devices
- Map phone localhost to laptop backend:
  adb reverse tcp:5000 tcp:5000
- Run app:
  flutter run -d <DEVICE_ID> --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000/api

7) Run app over Wi-Fi (no USB)
- Connect laptop and phone to same Wi-Fi
- Find laptop IP (example 192.168.1.6):
  ipconfig
- Ensure backend is running on laptop
- Allow firewall for TCP 5000 if needed
- Run Flutter directly with Wi-Fi backend URL:
  flutter run -d <DEVICE_ID> --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://<LAPTOP_IP>:5000/api

8) Build APK for install on phone
- cd flutter_app
- flutter clean
- flutter pub get
- flutter build apk --release --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://<LAPTOP_IP>:5000/api
- APK output:
  build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk

9) Install APK on phone
- Transfer app-release.apk to phone
- Open APK and allow install from unknown source if prompted
- Keep backend + Ollama running on laptop while using app

10) Quick troubleshooting
- If you see "Source: unknown": update app to latest build and ensure backend is reachable
- If /ask-question returns 422: image OCR failed, retake a clearer nutrition-label photo
- If phone cannot connect over Wi-Fi: verify same network, IP, firewall, and backend running
- If Flutter loses device connection: run adb devices, reconnect USB, rerun flutter command
